From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 shutdown closes pages that cannot ask together

Bridge 0.71.0. ReArcEngineShutdown closed every tab one at a time through
close_controller: beforeunload, then ClosePage (a renderer round trip that
runs unload and pagehide, up to content's 500 ms timeout), then a posted
finalize and the contents destructor, before the next tab began. A quit
took the sum over all live tabs, ~35 ms each even when forced, far more
for busy background renderers. Chrome instead fast-shuts-down renderers
with no unload-time handler and closes its tabs together.

A non-forced shutdown now closes alone, in order, only the tabs whose page
may ask "Leave site?" (a beforeunload handler in a live frame) or whose
close is in flight, so Stay still keeps the engine running before any other
page unloads, and earlier closed tabs stay closed as before. Once none is
left, every other tab closes in one task, as Chrome's browser shutdown does
(browser_shutdown::OnShutdownStarting, TabStripModel::CloseWebContentses):
a renderer whose pages are all closing and have no unload, pagehide or
visibilitychange handler ends at once (FastShutdownIfPossible, reported as a
normal termination, so no tab shows crashed), and those pages are destroyed
without a round trip. Pages with such a handler still run it, in parallel.
A page that gained a beforeunload handler meanwhile is closed alone first.
A forced shutdown closes every tab in that one task and skips unload
handlers. Close replies of a vetoed shutdown carry its generation and do
not act on the next one. Nothing in the C ABI changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-13 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.100 (46876a0c2d).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

